;;; -*- Mode: Indented-Text; -*-
*			  Sep. 4, 1998 0.60
	- now compatible with Allegro CL 5.0beta for Linux
*			  Jul. 7, 1995 0.59
	- new version of defsystem for ACL 4.2
*			  Jan. 19, 1995 0.58
	- parsing rule for object defintion is fixed.  Thanks to Mr.Igarashi.
*			  Jan. 12, 1995 0.57
	- a bug in DO form is fixed.  Thanks to Mr.Igarashi.
*			  Dec. 14, 1994 0.56
	- where expressions are separated from script bodies
*			  Dec. 12, 1994 0.55
	- default group managers and metaobject generators now accept
	  extra parameters for object creation requesets.
*			  Jul. 28, 1994 0.54
	- an event handling mechanism is added.
	- odd features on lexical variables are documented.
*			  Jun. 2, 1994 0.53
	- minor mistake in NRM translator for CLISP is fixed
	- a bug for the evaluator replacement is fixed.
*			  May. 11, 1994 0.52
	- CLISP is now supported.
	- backquotes are no longer used to compose messages
	- an inheritance example is added
	- minor mistake in NRM translator for Allegro-CL is fixed
*			Oct. 9, 1993 0.51
	- Allegro CL is now supported
	- mcl2.0-environment is included.
*Gesi			Jun.21, 1993 0.50
	- special forms reify-args & reify-args-to-meta is added.
	- fixed bugs in reifying default kernel objects
	- bug fix to TimeWarp example.
*			Mar.27, 1993 0.43
		(some improvements and bug fixes)
	- paren.lisp that supports closing parenthesis in MCL.
	- LOOP is redefined as a macro to DO.
	- Listener window is created in MCL.
	- Internal expressions whose types are :SELF-EVAL, are
	  evaluated by FUNCALL, instead of EVAL.  Because of this
	  change, the definitions of the evaluators provided by the
	  system are changed slightly.
	- Under MCL, dialogical selection when the argument for the
	  function CD is omitted. 
*			Jan.28, 1993 0.42
	- promblems with FROM field of a NRM object is fixed.
*			Jan.26, 1993 0.41
		  (some improvements and bug fixes)
	- (LET ((X (PROGN 1))) X) now returns 1 not (PROGN 1).
	- EVAL-WHEN forms now can be used, but their bodies are executed at
	  any situation.
	- Restart facility (by typing :reset at the toplevel) is
	  added. 
	- In examlpes/misc/MCP.abclr2, the evaluator now can accept
	  messages with additional arguments.
	- In [group...], meta-gen and evaluator bocome optional.
	- A keyword RESOURCES for group definition is EXPORTed.
	- GROUP-OF form is added.
	- debugging libraries copy, report, and watch are developed.
	- the metaobject can change its evaluator.
	- lib/express.abclr2 now provides ABCL/1 compatible express messages.
*Rissyu			Nov.16, 1992 0.40
	- Finally, the User's Guide in English available.
	- CLOS constructs are now accepted.
	- definition for primary metaobjects is imporved.
	- deysystem.lsp is corrected for CMU-CL 16e.
	- user-script.abclr2 is corrected for unknown messages.
*			Aug.14, 1992 0.36
		   (pre-release of Rissyu version)
	- Package names are changed for Sun-CL
	- Interactive readtable for MCL2.0 is restored.
	- Minor bug fix; script for default metaobject was wrong.
*			Aug. 8, 1992 0.35.1
		   (pre-release of Rissyu version)
	- Minor bug fix; `global-env' in global environment
*			Aug. 8, 1992 0.35
		   (pre-release of Rissyu version)
	- User's Guide is written, though in Japanese.
	- Minor bug fix; e.g., Ignore `declare' form.
*			Jul.30, 1992 0.34
	- Context sensitive inc, inc-lib, and require&provide macros.
	- Scripts with WHERE constraints can be used. An object which
	  contains such scripts is generated by heavy-meta.
	- Script :scripts is added to primary metaobjects.
*			Jul.25, 1992 0.33
	- The initial value of global environment, which was given by
	  quote form, is modified to be created by pairlis.  This is
	  because destructive modification of quoted data (i.e.,
	  constant) is an error for CLtL2.
	- Error checking codes before sending messages, taking metas
	  are added.
*			Jul.21, 1992 0.32
	- Minor bug fix; parsing error detection, multiple-value
	  functions.
	- Multicast and express type messages can be sent.

*			Jul.17, 1992 0.31
	- Future type messages can be sent.
*Tanabata		Jul 7,'92, 0.3
	<internal version>
	- The system works on following Lisp systems:
	  o KCl (on SparcStations)
	  o AKCl (on SparcStations)
	  o CMU-CL v16c (on SparcStations)
	  o MCL v2.0b1p3 (on Macintoshes)
	- Error handling routines are added, though they are not
	satisfactory.
	- Directory management functions are enhanced.
	- Macros can be used now.
	- "Do" is implemented as a special form. (Dolist and dotimes
	  are also available by defining them as macros.)
	- The system now works under ABCLR2-SYSTEM package, and user
	defined functions and macros are stored into ABCLR2-USER
	package.
	- The system is now compiled and loaded by use of CMU's
	portable defsystem.
	- Following ABCL/1 features still remain to be implemented:
	  o express messages,
	  o multi-cast,
	  o future type messages,
	  o match-loop,
	  o routine call,
	  o some special forms of common lisp (block, declare, go,
	    multiple-value, return-from, and tagbody)
	  o suicide
	  o debugging commands (e.g., describe, inspect, protocol, and
	    trace)
*Vernal Equinox Day	3/20/92, 0.2
	<preliminary release>
	- Directory management functions (cd & pwd) are available.
	- but, many features are unsupported...
*Hinamatsuri 		3/3/92, 0.1{a,b,c}
	<pre-release version>
	- for TOP-1 CL, KCl, CMU-CL, and MACL
	- no error recovery, etc.
